{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775343739-ERm0w0gugmU2hSJd9z1v","role":"assistant","created":1775343766,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data I need. Let me extract the monthly judiciary outlays from January 1984 to March 1987.\n\nFrom the data files:\n- treasury_bulletin_1985_03_page_22.txt contains data for 1984 (fiscal year data)\n- treasury_bulletin_1986_03_page_26.txt contains data for 1984-1985\n- treasury_bulletin_1987_03_page_24.txt contains data for 1985-1986\n- treasury_bulletin_1988_03_page_36.txt contains data for 1986-1987\n\nLet me extract all the monthly data for The Judiciary from January 1984 to March 1987:\n\nFrom treasury_bulletin_1985_03_page_22.txt (1984 data, calendar year):\n- 1984-Jan: 84\n- 1984-Feb: 89\n- 1984-Mar: 63\n- 1984-Apr: 74\n- 1984-May: 62\n- 1984-June: 93\n- 1984-July: 65\n- 1984-Aug: 79\n- 1984-Sept: 69\n- 1984-Oct: 79\n- 1984-Nov: 67\n- 1984-Dec: 96\n\nFrom treasury_bulletin_1986_03_page_26.txt (1985 data):\n- 1985-Jan: 66\n- 1985-Feb: 60\n- 1985-Mar: 59\n- 1985-Apr: 119\n- 1985-May: 75\n- 1985-June: 63\n- 1985-July: 74\n- 1985-Aug: 103\n- 1985-Sept: 66\n- 1985-Oct: 98\n- 1985-Nov: 74\n- 1985-Dec: 102\n\n\n- 1986-Jan: 76\n- 1986-Feb: 109\n- 1986-Mar: 74\n\nI notice the treasury_bulletin_1987_03_page_24.txt appears to have incomplete monthly data for 1986. I'll need to locate additional data sources to fill in the remaining months of 1986 and early 1987 to complete my analysis.\n\nThe treasury_bulletin_1988_03_page_36.txt provides more comprehensive monthly outlay figures for The Judiciary spanning from January 1986 through December 1987. This will help me complete the dataset and ensure accurate calculations.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_8b55f5ce0e9a433ba646d6dd","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\nimport math\n\n# Extract monthly judiciary outlays from Jan 1984 to Mar 1987\n# Data from the Treasury Bulletin pages\n\n# From treasury_bulletin_1985_03_page_22.txt (1984 calendar year data)\noutlays_1984 = {\n    '1984-Jan': 84,\n    '1984-Feb': 89,\n    '1984-Mar': 63,\n    '1984-Apr': 74,\n    '1984-May': 62,\n    '1984-Jun': 93,\n    '1984-Jul': 65,\n    '1984-Aug': 79,\n    '1984-Sep': 69,\n    '1984-Oct': 79,\n    '1984-Nov': 67,\n    '1984-Dec': 96,\n}\n\n# From treasury_bulletin_1986_03_page_26.txt (1985 data - fiscal year starting Oct 1984)\noutlays_1985 = {\n    '1985-Jan': 66,\n    '1985-Feb': 60,\n    '1985-Mar': 59,\n    '1985-Apr': 119,\n    '1985-May': 75,\n    '1985-Jun': 63,\n    '1985-Jul': 74,\n    '1985-Aug': 103,\n    '1985-Sep': 66,\n    '1985-Oct': 98,\n    '1985-Nov': 74,\n    '1985-Dec': 102,\n}\n\n# From treasury_bulletin_1987_03_page_24.txt and treasury_bulletin_1988_03_page_36.txt (1986-1987)\noutlays_1986 = {\n    '1986-Jan': 76,\n    '1986-Feb': 109,\n    '1986-Mar': 74,\n    '1986-Apr': 129,\n    '1986-May': 75,\n    '1986-Jun': 71,\n    '1986-Jul': 70,\n    '1986-Aug': 106,\n    '1986-Sep': 87,\n    '1986-Oct': 73,\n    '1986-Nov': 73,\n    '1986-Dec': 113,\n}\n\noutlays_1987 = {\n    '1987-Jan': 79,\n    '1987-Feb': 76,\n    '1987-Mar': 110,\n}\n\n# Combine all data from Jan 1984 to Mar 1987\nall_outlays = []\n\n# 1984 months\nfor month in ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec']:\n    all_outlays.append(outlays_1984[f'1984-{month}'])\n\n# 1985 months\nfor month in ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec']:\n    all_outlays.append(outlays_1985[f'1985-{month}'])\n\n# 1986 months\nfor month in ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar', 'Apr', 'May', 'Jun', 'Jul', 'Aug', 'Sep', 'Oct', 'Nov', 'Dec']:\n    all_outlays.append(outlays_1986[f'1986-{month}'])\n\n# 1987 Jan-Mar\nfor month in ['Jan', 'Feb', 'Mar']:\n    all_outlays.append(outlays_1987[f'1987-{month}'])\n\nprint(f\"Number of months: {len(all_outlays)}\")\nprint(f\"Outlays: {all_outlays}\")\n\n# Calculate geometric mean\n# GM = (product of all values)^(1/n)\nlog_sum = sum(math.log(x) for x in all_outlays)\ngeometric_mean = math.exp(log_sum / len(all_outlays))\n\nprint(f\"\\nGeometric mean: {geometric_mean}\")\nprint(f\"Geometric mean in millions (rounded to thousandth): {round(geometric_mean, 3)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
