{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775343889-WaaYArQJc1y7gJQTtAOC","role":"assistant","created":1775343912,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see the issue. After 1984-Jan, the subsequent months (Feb, Mar, etc.) don't have the year prefix - they just have \"Feb.\", \"Mar.\", etc. The first row has \"1984-Jan.\" and then subsequent rows have just the month.\n\nLooking at the data:\n- 1984-Jan: 84\n- Feb: 89\n- Mar: 63\n- Apr: 74\n- May: 62\n- June: 93\n- July: 65\n- Aug: 79\n- Sept: 69\n- Oct: 79\n- Nov: 67\n- Dec: 96\n\nSo I need to handle this differently - extract all the month values after 1984-Jan until the next year starts.\n\nLet me look at all the data more systematically:\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_408dd94516a54577b123b57e","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Now I understand - after the first month with year, subsequent months just have month name\n# Let me extract all the data properly\n\ndef extract_all_monthly_data(content):\n    \"\"\"Extract all monthly judiciary data from a table\"\"\"\n    import re\n    \n    tables = content.split('<table>')\n    \n    # Find the table with monthly data\n    target_table = None\n    for table in tables:\n        if 'The Judiciary' in table and ('Jan' in table or 'Feb' in table):\n            target_table = table\n            break\n    \n    if not target_table:\n        return {}\n    \n    # Extract rows with month data\n    # Pattern: <td>year-Month.</td> or <td>Month.</td>\n    # The Judiciary column is the 3rd column (index 2)\n    \n    # First, find all rows with either \"year-Month.\" or just \"Month.\" pattern\n    # and extract the 3rd numeric value\n    \n    values = []\n    \n    # Split into rows\n    rows = target_table.split('</tr>')\n    \n    current_year = None\n    for row in rows:\n        # Check for year pattern first: <td>1984-Jan.</td>\n        year_match = re.search(r'<td>(\\d{4})-(Jan|Feb|Mar|Apr|May|Jun|Jul|Aug|Sep|Oct|Nov|Dec)\\.</td>', row)\n        if year_match:\n            current_year = year_match.group(1)\n            # Extract judiciary value (3rd numeric column)\n            nums = re.findall(r'<td>([\\d,]+)</td>', row)\n            if len(nums) >= 3:\n                # Remove commas and convert to int\n                val = int(nums[2].replace(',', ''))\n                values.append((f\"{current_year}-{year_match.group(2)}\", val))\n            continue\n        \n        # Check for month-only pattern: <td>Jan.</td> etc\n        month_match = re.search(r'<td>(Jan|Feb|Mar|Apr|May|Jun|Jul|Aug|Sep|Oct|Nov|Dec)\\.?</td>', row)\n        if month_match and current_year:\n            # Extract judiciary value\n            nums = re.findall(r'<td>([\\d,]+)</td>', row)\n            if len(nums) >= 3:\n                val = int(nums[2].replace(',', ''))\n                values.append((f\"{current_year}-{month_match.group(1)}\", val))\n    \n    return dict(values)\n\n# Test with 1985 bulletin\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1985_03_page_22.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content_1985 = f.read()\n\nprint(\"=== 1984 data (from 1985 bulletin) ===\")\ndata_1984 = extract_all_monthly_data(content_1985)\nfor k, v in sorted(data_1984.items()):\n    print(f\"{k}: {v}\")\n\n# Now 1985 from 1986 bulletin\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1986_03_page_26.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content_1986 = f.read()\n\nprint(\"\\n=== 1985 data (from 1986 bulletin) ===\")\ndata_1985 = extract_all_monthly_data(content_1986)\nfor k, v in sorted(data_1985.items()):\n    print(f\"{k}: {v}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
